WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:07.200
Lebanon has been plunged into darkness, after&nbsp;
its two largest power stations were shut down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.800
due to a prolonged fuel shortage. Officials&nbsp;
say the outage will last several days.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.560
It's the latest hardship for people&nbsp;
in Lebanon, where three-quarters of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.280
the population are in poverty due to&nbsp;
soaring prices and record unemployment.&nbsp;

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:29.120
Financial crisis has kept Lebanon’s economy&nbsp;
in the red. And now fuel shortages have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:35.280
plunged the entire country into darkness.
"The electricity used to be cut off for three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:45.120
hours. Then recently, we only had three hours&nbsp;
of electricity. Now, there is none at all.”&nbsp;

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.640
First the power went out at the Deir Ammar&nbsp;
plant. Then the Zahrani plant went offline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.120
The outages caused Lebanon’s centrally&nbsp;
generated electrical grid to collapse.&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.680
"We are spending our time outside our&nbsp;
homes, so our children can have fun.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:05.440
The situation is getting steadily worse.&nbsp;
May God protect us from what's coming next."&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.520
Many people have come to depend on&nbsp;
private generators that run on diesel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.600
but that is in short supply&nbsp;
too and it, like most goods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.960
is becoming pricey. Since 2019, the&nbsp;
Lebanese currency has dropped 90%.&nbsp;

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.320
This outage has added more weight to&nbsp;
the burden people must carry here.&nbsp;

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.360
"It's affecting me, my house is on the&nbsp;
eleventh floor, I can't go up or down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.360
sometimes I sleep in the car until 3 or 4&nbsp;
am, so there might be electricity, what can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:41.440
we do? Look at the life we're living."
The army has agreed to provide 6,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:53.840
kiloliters of gas oil, securing&nbsp;
power in Lebanon for just three days.

